"Tutorial text (arrow boundary)" = "
Use the always hidden feature to keep your icons tidy. Here's how to set it
Steps to enable:
1. Enable the always hidden “|” (translucent color bar)
2. Hold  ⌘ and drag it to the left of the arrow, then move any icons you want to disappear on the left of that bar.
3. Finally, hold ⌥ Option and click the collapse “<” icon to make it disappear.
Steps to view always hidden icons:
1. Option-click the “<” icon again to view and repeat the action to enable the feature. Enjoy 😉!
";
